  "notes": "The three-character floor excludes almost the whole stock of two-kanji Japanese policy words (削減, 廃止, 凍結, 禁止, 延長, 導入, 備蓄, 措置, 給付, 課税), so each sense is carried instead by its ~する / ~した / ~ている-stem form and by four-character compounds (規制緩和, 備蓄放出, 緊急事態宣言, 一時停止). Bare 会, 措置, 対策 were also avoided as substrings of everyday words such as 記者会見 and 株式会社. Fuel-specific instruments 揮発油税, 石油石炭税 and the ガソリン補助金 wording were dropped because they embed subject nouns; 激変緩和措置, the actual name of the Japanese fuel subsidy, is kept because it names only the instrument."
